==German==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈmɔɐ̯ɡŋ̩]|[ˈmɔɐ̯ɡən]|[ˈmɔʁɡŋ̩]|[ˈmɔʁɡən]|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-Morgen.ogg|audio|lang=de}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|morgen|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|morgan|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*murganaz}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*mr̥Hko||to blink, twinkle}}. Compare Low German {{term|Morgen|lang=nds}}, Dutch {{term|morgen|lang=nl}}, West Frisian {{term|moarn|lang=fy}}, English {{term|morn|lang=en}}, {{term|morrow|lang=en}}, Danish {{term|morgen|lang=da}}, Swedish {{term|morgon|lang=sv}}.

====Noun====
{{de-noun|m|Morgens|Morgen|pl2=Morgende}}

# [[morning]]
# [[morgen]] (measure of land)

=====Usage notes=====
* The normal plural is unchanged '''''Morgen'''''.
* The plural ''Morgende'' is of dialectal origin. It is rather common colloquially but rarely ever used in literary German.

